      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Inflation and the quantum origin of structure give a compelling, unifying account of the early universe and make the observed cosmos intelligible.",
        "attribution": "Guth introduced inflation, Linde developed its enduring theoretical forms, and Mukhanov established the quantum-perturbation mechanism connecting it to structure.",
        "maturity": "Multiple cosmological observations strongly support its principal consequences; the idea has shaped cosmology for decades.",
