        "nobel_worthiness": "Horizon-scale imaging of a black hole is an extraordinary observational achievement, making strong-gravity phenomena accessible in a new way.",
        "attribution": "Falcke drove the imaging vision, Doeleman led the Event Horizon Telescope realization, and Zensus was a major architect of the radio-interferometric effort.",
        "maturity": "The result has been reproduced for a second black hole and has established a durable observational field.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The result depends on a large collaboration, and individual attribution is necessarily selective."
        ]
      }
    },
